{"seq":11,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-installer-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T16:15:42.623Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"9a437c8d1c4be7da47cfe97f9b11006b6fae4f71af8b455109f6497df965ba6e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines (QFL) ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#4419**: Gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Source: Moss's North cheat sheet (undated). It says Thea Ramaswell logged it, and that it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n2. **#4419 (again)**: Listed as \"Gate 3 printer lag\" (BOL printout delay), with a patch pushed and a follow-up to Thea still open. Source: Marcus Lindqvist's \"Q2 expansion wrap (belated),\" dated 14 Jul 2025. The number matches #4419 above, but the description differs, so someone should confirm whether these are the same ticket.\n3. **#PD-4492**: Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts. Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025, support patched it, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct was clear. Source: Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth,\" 5 Oct 2025.\n\nLeft out on purpose:\n- **#4092** (IT, Zoom Room hub) and **#4409 / #4412** (Pree/Marrow Central account) are not QFL tickets.\n- The #inc-qfl-sev1 war room (4 Nov 2025) mentions no ticket number.\n\nThis search is keyword-only, so a note that refers to QFL without the name or a ticket number could have been missed. I can also write this list into a weekly notes file if you tell me where it should go."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
